### The list of files with no transcript

Each file the sheet reads that has no filler transcript gets a row, under the heading "Filler words are found only in an AssemblyAI transcript made with filler words — transcription on this Mac does not report them. These files have none yet:". The whole section is hidden when ev

A row has the file's name, an estimate and a **Transcribe** button. The estimate reads, for example:

`1 file to upload · 00:00:05.249 of audio · under $0.01 at AssemblyAI's published rate`

The upload is the whole file's audio, not only the part your clips play. Rest the pointer on the estimate to see the rate. It's $0.21 an hour, or $0.23 an hour when the file's earlier transcript used speaker labels.

The list covers [the same clips as the rest of the sheet](/cleanup/remove-filler-words/#which-clips-are-read): the selected clips when the selection holds a clip Frame Job can read, otherwise every clip. A file is listed only if one of those clips plays its sound. Clips that play

### Where the audio goes

Above the rows, the sheet says where the audio goes before anything is sent:

- You can transcribe a project you haven't saved yet. Its transcript is kept with the project when you save.
- AssemblyAI takes up to 10 hours in one file. Frame Job says so in the note before it uploads anything.
- If AssemblyAI hasn't confirmed deleting an earlier transcript of a file, the row reads "Nothing to upload · 1 file waiting on an earlier delete". **Transcribe** tries that delete again first. If it goes through, the file uploads as normal. If it doesn't, nothing is uploaded and the note says why.
- If AssemblyAI rejects your key, the note reads "AssemblyAI refused the API key — check it in Frame Job ▸ Settings".

## With an agent
Two more counts can appear, and neither is in the price:

| The line says | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| "1 file waiting on an earlier delete" | The file [isn't uploaded](/captions/assemblyai-privacy/#a-pending-delete-holds-a-file-back) until AssemblyAI confirms an earlier delete. |
| "1 file could not be read" | Frame Job couldn't read the media file, so it can't be transcribed. With nothing else to do, **Generate** is greyed. |

## Why each file uploads

Rest the pointer on the summary line. You get one line for each file that isn't already transcribed, saying why, and then the rate as a dated sentence.

| The line says | What changed |
| --- | --- |
| "has not been transcribed yet" | This file has no transcript in the project. |
| "has changed since it was transcribed" | The file on disk isn't the one that was transcribed. |
| "was transcribed with a different language" | The named setting differs from the transcript's. It can also name **model**, **speakers** or **vocabulary**, or several of them. |
| "was transcribed for a different request" | Something else about the request differs. |
| "is already transcribed, and Transcribe again was asked for" | You ticked [Transcribe again](#transcribe-again). |
| "could not be read, so it cannot be transcribed" | The media file couldn't be read. |

